{"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"TaskLoom"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Cancellation and retries"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/TaskLoom\/documentation\/TaskLoom"]]},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"Understand policy ordering and cooperative cancellation before composing work.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/taskloom\/cancellationandretries"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Guides","title":"Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TaskLoom\/documentation\/TaskLoom\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/TaskLoom\/documentation\/TaskLoom\/TaskLifetimes","doc:\/\/TaskLoom\/documentation\/TaskLoom\/CombineAndDispatch","doc:\/\/TaskLoom\/documentation\/TaskLoom\/DebuggingAndTesting","doc:\/\/TaskLoom\/documentation\/TaskLoom\/ConcurrentWork"],"generated":true}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Policy-order","text":"Policy order","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Modifiers wrap the operation built so far. "},{"code":".retry(3).timeout(.seconds(5))","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" gives the whole sequence a five-second timeout. "},{"code":".timeout(.seconds(5)).retry(3)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" gives each attempt its own timeout. The retry count includes the initial attempt and must be positive."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TaskLoom\/documentation\/TaskLoom\/BackoffStrategy","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" provides constant, linear, exponential, jittered exponential, and custom delays. Exhausted retries throw "},{"code":"AsyncOperationError.maxRetriesExceeded","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", preserving the last error. Cancellation is checked before each attempt and before backoff. Cancellation errors never retry. Use "},{"code":"retry(_:backoff:when:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to select eligible failures; rejected errors propagate unchanged."}]},{"anchor":"Cooperative-timeouts","text":"Cooperative timeouts","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Timeouts race work against a sleeping child task. The losing child is cancelled, but the task group must wait for every child to exit. A timeout is therefore a cancellation request, not a guarantee that the function returns at a wall-clock deadline. Use cancellation-aware suspension points and "},{"code":"Task.checkCancellation()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in long-running work."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TaskLoom\/documentation\/TaskLoom\/AsyncTask","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" expresses timeouts with a default value. It cannot throw "},{"code":"CancellationError","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to its caller. Converting an operation with "},{"code":"toTask(default:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" also turns all errors, including cancellation, into the supplied default."}]},{"anchor":"Races-and-fallback","text":"Races and fallback","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"AsyncOperation.race","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" uses the first completed result, which may be an error. It does not wait for the first success after an earlier failure. Losing child tasks are cancelled cooperatively."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"fallback","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"recover","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" propagate "},{"code":"CancellationError","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"AsyncOperationError.cancelled","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and the current task’s cancellation state. "},{"code":"recover","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" receives ordinary errors so it can select a replacement value. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"checkCancellation()"},{"type":"text","text":" checks immediately before starting its wrapped work; it does not automatically insert checks inside your closure."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"allSettled"},{"type":"text","text":" retains one "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Result"},{"type":"text","text":" for every input in input order. Individual child failures, including child cancellation errors, become results; cancellation of the parent cancels the group and throws. Choose "},{"code":"all","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" when an unsuccessful child must fail the overall operation."}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"Injectable-timing","type":"heading","text":"Injectable timing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Timeouts and retries accept "},{"code":"clock:","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" overloads. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DelayedTask"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RepeatingTask"},{"type":"text","text":" accept "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Duration"},{"type":"text","text":" plus "},{"code":"clock:","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; their handlers remain on the main actor. A throwing delayed task propagates cancellation. See "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TaskLoom\/documentation\/TaskLoom\/DebuggingAndTesting"},{"type":"text","text":" for deterministic tests."}]}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/TaskLoom\/documentation\/TaskLoom\/CancellationAndRetries"},"kind":"article","references":{"doc://TaskLoom/documentation/TaskLoom/AsyncTask":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TaskLoom\/documentation\/TaskLoom\/AsyncTask","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A composable, lazy async task that cannot fail."}],"title":"AsyncTask","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/taskloom\/asynctask","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AsyncTask"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AsyncTask"}]},"doc://TaskLoom/documentation/TaskLoom/BackoffStrategy":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"BackoffStrategy","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Defines strategies for calculating delay between retry attempts.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BackoffStrategy","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/TaskLoom\/documentation\/TaskLoom\/BackoffStrategy","title":"BackoffStrategy","url":"\/documentation\/taskloom\/backoffstrategy","kind":"symbol"},"doc://TaskLoom/documentation/TaskLoom/CombineAndDispatch":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TaskLoom\/documentation\/TaskLoom\/CombineAndDispatch","abstract":[{"text":"Use the platform bridges alongside the portable concurrency APIs.","type":"text"}],"title":"Combine and Dispatch","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/taskloom\/combineanddispatch","kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://TaskLoom/documentation/TaskLoom/ConcurrentWork":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TaskLoom\/documentation\/TaskLoom\/ConcurrentWork","abstract":[{"text":"Bound batch processing and prevent outdated requests from updating UI state.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/taskloom\/concurrentwork","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Concurrent work"},"doc://TaskLoom/documentation/TaskLoom/GettingStarted":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TaskLoom\/documentation\/TaskLoom\/GettingStarted","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Build a reusable asynchronous operation and choose the policies that surround it."}],"title":"Getting started","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/taskloom\/gettingstarted","kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://TaskLoom/documentation/TaskLoom":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TaskLoom\/documentation\/TaskLoom","abstract":[{"text":"Compose asynchronous work, manage task lifetimes, and bridge Swift concurrency with Combine.","type":"text"}],"title":"TaskLoom","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/taskloom","kind":"symbol","role":"collection"},"doc://TaskLoom/documentation/TaskLoom/TaskLifetimes":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TaskLoom\/documentation\/TaskLoom\/TaskLifetimes","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Keep ownership explicit when creating and retaining asynchronous work."}],"title":"Task lifetimes","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/taskloom\/tasklifetimes","type":"topic","role":"article"},"doc://TaskLoom/documentation/TaskLoom/DebuggingAndTesting":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TaskLoom\/documentation\/TaskLoom\/DebuggingAndTesting","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Name operations, inspect their lifecycle, and advance time explicitly in tests."}],"title":"Debugging and testing","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/taskloom\/debuggingandtesting","kind":"article","role":"article"}}}